%description:

Tcp.ecnMarkAll:all -- the pure ACKs of an AccECN connection are ECT(0).

The claim (Tcp.ned): "ECN: ECT also on the pure ACKs, FINs, retransmissions and window probes of
an AccECN connection (RFC 9768) and of a DCTCP connection, as Linux does ...; false: ECT only on
new data, as RFC 3168 sections 6.1.4 to 6.1.6 ask".

The classes: new-data (false, the default) and all (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::sendToIP() sets ECT(0) only on new data with false; with true, also on the pure
ACKs, FINs, retransmissions and window probes of an AccECN or a DCTCP connection. This test separates "all" from the other value.

Host under test: host2, the receiver of an AccECN connection (tcpEcnMode "accecn-passive"; host1
"accecn": preconditions), which sends only pure ACKs. Observation: level 1, the first pure ACK
of host2 after the handshake reaches host1 with the IP ECN field ECT(0).

%# parameter: Tcp.ecnMarkAll
%# class: all
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.ecnMarkAll
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpEcnMarkAllAll")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackNo > {isn} + 1")
                  .first()
                  .assertPacket("ipv4.ecn == 2")
                  .describe("the first ACK of data of host2 at host1")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpEcnMarkAllAll compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.ecnMarkAll = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.host2.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn-passive"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpEcnMarkAllAll: PASS
